WEBVTT

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.730
<i>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!</i>

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.410
<i>It involves playing 
rock-paper-scissors with 12 cards</i>

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:19.180
<i>while trying to win each other's stars. 
It might seem like a game of chance,</i>

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.660
<i>and yet...</i>

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.370
<i>Once cards are played, they are discarded.</i>

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.890
<i>The total number is counted,</i>

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.460
<i>so strategy is necessary in 
choosing when to play each card.</i>

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.790
<i>Not only that, but there 
is a four-hour time limit!</i>

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.530
<i>You need to obtain more than three 
stars during the time limit</i>

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.970
<i>and use up all your cards, or you lose!</i>

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.860
<i>Deception! Competition! Betrayal!</i>

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.480
<i>You need to have what it 
takes to leave others behind.</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.100
<i>A truly diabolical game!</i>

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:52.030
<i>And now... we turn back the clock.</i>

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.030
Tonegawa-sensei.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.780
The digital scoreboard is here!

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.040
Good.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:00.510
Sensei!

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:01.290
The tables, too!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.000
Good, they're here.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:07.320
<i>One week before the first rehearsal game 
of Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors,</i>

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.000
<i>the requested equipment is delivered, 
one piece after another.</i>

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.010
Looks like we've got everything we 
need for the game, more or less.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.010
Let's try putting a card in.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.900
<b>Mmmm...</b>

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:29.900
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.900
Hey. The count's not going down.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:33.960
Huh?

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.590
Don't "huh" me.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.490
For Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors, each play

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:45.240
is supposed to be tracked, and the number 
of remaining cards accurately displayed.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.670
The cards have some kind of chip 
embedded in them, don't they?

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.620
Wh-Who put the chips in?

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:53.840
Who did it?

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.340
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.140
<b>Psst...</b>

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.140
Don't tell me... you people...

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:06.640
<b>Cards</b>

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.050
You're telling me all these 
cards... They're just paper?

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.640
Useless paper waste? Surely not, right?

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:10.150
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:12.150
You stupid...

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:17.150
N-No. The table, at least, 
has to have something, right?

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.160
It's empty?! Totally empty?!

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.240
W-We're so sorry, sir! We'll order 
a new batch of cards right away!

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.470
There's no time!

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.790
At this point, you fools will fix this

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.300
by counting the cards yourselves! 
<i>Inside</i> the tables!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.800
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.730
I-Inside them?

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:41.610
We can't do that!

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:42.680
That's impossible!

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.680
Being inside a tiny space like that for 
four hours would drive anybody crazy!

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.740
What about food? What are we 
supposed to do if we get hungry?

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.810
That's right, sir!

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:55.620
It's not just our stomachs! 
Think of the havoc it'll wreak!

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.510
On our backs!

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:57.820
Impossible!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.320
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.320
<b>Cards    Stars</b>

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.860
I get it. Fine, then.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.960
Can't do this, can't do that...

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.960
I've had enough. You people can figure it out.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:30.060
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:30.060
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.810
<i>Agenda 10
</i>Rehearsal

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.880
<i>Well, now that I really think about it,</i>

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.040
<i>if we head to the manufacturers 
and press the issue,</i>

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:03.120
<i>we can still make it in time 
for rehearsal next week.</i>

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:09.610
<i>Even if I was justifiably upset, asking them 
to get inside the tables was a bit much.</i>

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.790
<i>I suppose I'll let them off the hook now.</i>

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:21.770
It's me.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:25.920
<i>Tonegawa-sensei! 
I was just about to call you.</i>

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.930
<i>Could you come to the big 
vacant room on the fifth floor?</i>

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.730
<b>Kawasaki</b>

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.730
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:43.920
<b>5F: Vacant Room</b>

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.190
Good to see you, Tonegawa-sensei.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.400
Yamazaki, what is all this?!

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:51.190
For now, try inserting a card, 
any card, into any table.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.810
<b>Gonda</b>

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:01.610
All right... How about this one?

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:06.920
<b>Psst...</b>

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:09.550
It was possible!

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.050
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:15.060
Our human scoreboard is active!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.060
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:23.070
Are you telling me that there 
are men in these tables?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.500
<b>Nagata

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.620
They've been in there for more 
or less five hours at this point,

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.070
<b>Hagio

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.070
and no one has bailed out.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.100
F-Five hours?!

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:31.820
What do you think?

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:37.100
I don't know what to say... I didn't 
think you'd be able to pull it off.

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:39.920
Indeed... I see it now.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.810
How dedicated you all are, and your grit!

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:44.920
But that's enough. You can come out now.

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:47.880
Wha?!

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:53.880
Oh, Sensei.

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:57.490
Saemon's theme is "relaxation."

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:01.540
He's got a low-resistance cushion to 
sit on and the latest gaming hardware.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:07.650
He's done a great job of recreating his 
room in this small 1.3 square meter space.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.410
This one's next!

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.410
<b>Gonda</b>

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.660
Oh, welcome, sir.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.910
<b>Ogino</b>

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:17.910
Gonda-san's theme is "dreams."

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:22.920
His old dream of owning a used 
bookstore has been recreated!

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:25.670
Nakata-san's theme is "The Cosmos."

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.920
Hey! Put the top back on!

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.510
Hagio-san's had what 
I think is the best idea.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:33.460
A cat café!

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:34.890
I-I see...

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.410
Is that something or what?!

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:39.730
Y-Yeah, it's... certainly something.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.720
<i>The men in black have 
overcome an impossible task,</i>

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:46.840
<i>but Tonegawa feels overwhelmingly... vexed.</i>

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.500
<b>Vex... Vex...</b>

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:52.090
Just... make sure the cats 
don't make too much noise.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:54.190
I'll try, sir.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.580
<i>He doesn't get angry! Just... vexed.</i>

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:59.120
<b>Vex... Vex...</b>

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.700
<b>Vex... Vex...</b>

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:08.060
<i>And so, a week later, the rookie men in 
black of Teiai are escorted to the </i>Espoir<i>.</i>

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:09.430
<i>The time has come!</i>

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:12.280
<i>For the diabolical project,</i>

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:16.810
<i>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors' 
first-ever... rehearsal!</i>

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.650
That concludes the explanation of the rules.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:23.320
This might be a rehearsal, but keep in mind, 
you're supposed to be in the pit of hell.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.980
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:31.350
Your objective here should be to win. 
Win, and escape this place.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:37.190
I want you all to act like you're in severe 
debt, and do your best to get clear.

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:37.990
Yes, sir!

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.750
Now, then...

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:55.050
Our diabolical strategy game, where the 
quick-witted will leave the rest to perish...

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:57.790
How will it play out?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.760
<i>However!</i>

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.760
<b>However...!</b>

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:03.770
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.700
Would you play a game with me?

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:07.400
Sure.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.900
Check. Set. Open!

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.570
I win.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:13.400
Right.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.390
Here's your star chip.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.400
Thank you. Maybe we'll play again.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:20.980
It's been a pleasure. Thank you.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:25.560
<i>Excuse me, do you know where the restroom is?</i>

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.110
<i>Let me pass you a star chip.</i>

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:29.200
<i>Oh, you dropped this.</i>

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:30.170
<i>I'm so sorry!</i>

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:33.670
<i>This is... a little too crisp.</i>

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:38.410
<i>I thought this would be a good 
training exercise for the new hires,</i>

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.180
<i>but they're still too stiff.</i>

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:47.190
<i>I could probably change the atmosphere 
by sending in a few of my team,</i>

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:50.090
<i>but they're all inside the tables...</i>

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.200
<i>I never anticipated this problem! 
At this rate...</i>

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.450
They have no clue how to act like debtors.

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:08.800
I heard your little program here 
was going to be interesting,

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:10.910
but from what I've seen...

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:23.970
<b>Teiai Subsidy
Endou Finance President
Endou Yuuji</b>

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.470
<i>A local loan shark under 
the employee of Teiai,</i>

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:16.990
<i>Endou Yuuji, the president of Endou Finance!</i>

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:20.490
<i>He would be the key man in the 
eventual collision between</i>

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:23.970
<i>Tonegawa and the legendary Itou Kaiji!</i>

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:28.430
Tonegawa-san... New employees 
are more afraid of screwing up

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:31.600
or embarrassing themselves than anything.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.730
They'll never be more 
anxious than they are now.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:37.420
Expecting them to play the 
debauched and unproductive,

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:41.130
their polar opposites, people in deep debt,

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:44.740
is not something you can pull off 
overnight. I'd say it's impossible!

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:50.180
Though, perhaps someone who's 
dealt with countless debtors before...

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:53.790
a lecture from a pro, let's say... 
could turn them around.

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:55.780
What are you getting at?

00:10:56.950 --> 00:11:01.000
Could you let me handle your 
men in black for a day?

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:08.060
I'll be able to turn them into authentic 
heavy debtors in a single day.

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:10.810
<i>And so...</i>

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:16.320
<i>The curtain rises on Endou's 
heavy debtor lecture!</i>

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:20.070
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:23.660
Now, what image do you all 
have when you think of

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.640
someone with multiple sources of debt?

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:27.830
How about you, over there?

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:32.830
R-Right! Well, this might be 
a bit crude, but... scumbags?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.700
Exactly right!

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:39.720
But the actual debtors can't even be 
accurately described as "scumbags."

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:44.850
They're more perplexing... and always choose 
the action that makes the least sense!

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:50.120
But me telling you about it 
probably won't be as simple as

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:52.750
letting you hear it straight 
from the horse's mouth.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:54.230
The horse's mouth?

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.110
Hello.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.110
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:20.760
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:16.110
Let me introduce you. Here's someone 
who's 3,800,000 yen in debt,

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:19.290
someone whose multiple cases of debt 
currently show signs of ongoing growth.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.880
This is Watanabe-kun.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.190
I'm Watanabe.

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:26.760
<b>Droop... Droop...</b>

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:26.760
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:33.520
I'm going to ask questions that 
demonstrate how much of a scumbag he is,

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.780
so I want you all to consider his answers

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:39.390
as you gain insight into the mind 
of someone in this kind of debt.

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:42.490
And so... first question.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.630
Despite how he appears, Watanabe-kun

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:48.030
used to have a job, thanks to some 
connections he had through a relative.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:52.540
However, it was soon found out that he 
had blown company money playing pachinko,

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:56.040
and he received an order from his boss 
to return to the office immediately.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:13:00.550
Now, then... What do you 
think Watanabe-kun did?

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.760
Sir! He headed straight back 
to the office and begged for—

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:05.340
Bzzt, nope.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:09.410
He went home to try and 
avoid the problem, perhaps?

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:12.620
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:11.730
Come on, no one would do that.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:14.650
Watanabe-kun, if you'd enlighten them.

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:15.450
Okay.

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:19.440
I rode the Yamanote line 
until the trains stopped.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:25.070
<b>Psst...</b>

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.640
The Yamanote line?

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:23.260
Just... around and around?

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:24.540
Oh, come on!

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:30.200
That's crazy! Going home would waste 
less time than that kind of thing!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:34.120
Well, I'd feel guilty if I went home,

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:38.240
but I didn't want to go to work 
either, so... what else could I do?

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:39.960
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:41.460
Question number two!

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:44.300
In an attempt to pay off 
Watanabe-kun's debts,

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.460
his mother borrowed money 
from the entire family,

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:48.970
totaling two million yen.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:55.230
Watanabe-kun took that money to 
the horse track and lost all of it.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:59.230
Now, why do you suppose he did such a thing?

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.070
I mean, more than asking why...

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:04.170
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:01.970
He's just crazy.

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:04.730
I know! Maybe he thought he could 
win and increase the amount?

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:07.520
Watanabe-kun?

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.510
Well, horse racing is a hobby of mine.

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:12.240
I like horses, y'know.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:17.000
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:17.000
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Where do hobbies or 
what you like even enter the equation?!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:23.480
Well, around that time, I had caught a cold, 
lost my keys... lots of bad stuff.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:28.010
I figured it'd be a nice change of pace, 
or maybe just a treat for myself.

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:34.990
We're not done yet, either. Question three!

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:41.650
<i>And ultimately, after several hours, 
Endou's debtor lecture finally concluded.</i>

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:44.150
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:44.150
<i>The next day...</i>

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:48.900
<i>The second day of the Restricted 
Rock-Paper-Scissors rehearsal!</i>

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:52.290
Morning, sir.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:54.700
Endou. How'd it go?

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:58.030
The only word that comes to mind is "perfect."

00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:03.160
They've all completely 
transformed into heavy debtors.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.340
Looks like they're here, too.

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:09.340
Look at that pack of losers.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:22.020
<b>Psst...</b>

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.330
Psst. Psst.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.030
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:37.660
<b>Meh... Meh... Meh...</b>

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:33.090
Now, listen up... I know it's a rehearsal, 
but treat it like it's the real deal,

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:35.940
and do all you can to make this authentic.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.660
Why?

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:41.410
Why should we do all we can?

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:48.050
<i>I see. This really is scum-like.</i>

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.670
<i>Just what I'd expect a scumbag to say!</i>

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:54.180
<i>They've made this rehearsal more real than 
I could've hoped for. Well done, Endou!</i>

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:58.360
'Scuse me...

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:01.430
I've got a stomachache. Can I go?

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:03.400
Me, too.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:03.960
Me, three.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:04.760
Same.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:07.440
<i>Be that as it may, the air is cleared...</i>

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:10.940
<i>And the rehearsal's second day begins!</i>

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:12.450
<i>However!</i>

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:12.450
<b>However...!</b>

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.740
One, two, three, four...

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:20.700
<b>Your pet is in a
popular commercial and
becomes a celebrity!
Win $5,000.</b>

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:20.700
"Your pet is in a popular commercial 
and becomes a celebrity. Win $5,000."

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:23.160
Yes! 5,000 bucks.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.710
Here you go, from the bank.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:32.220
Wh-What the hell are they doing?

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:33.840
Playing a board game, sir.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:35.070
I can see that!

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.430
Fine, then... Ton!

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:37.970
Sir?

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:40.470
Bring the stuff.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.770
<i>A few minutes later...</i>

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:47.050
Now, there was something I forgot to mention.

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:51.530
For the first ten players to finish 
our Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors,

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:55.450
we have this gift: 
a specially made Teiai clear file!

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:59.030
<b>We're always by your side
Teiai Finance</b>

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:59.030
<i>Tonegawa uses merchandise 
to attempt to motivate!</i>

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.290
<b>However...!</b>

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.290
<i>However!</i>

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:01.980
<i>There's no effect!</i>

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.900
<i>They show less than no interest.</i>

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:06.580
Payday...

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.510
You want any stocks?

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:08.040
Sure...

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:10.550
I-In that case...

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:15.050
The clear file and this special kuo card!

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.550
Good for 1,000 yen!

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:22.060
Sweet, I won the lottery. 200,000 bucks.

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:25.090
<i>Their interest is fading at a diabolical speed!</i>

00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:27.560
<i>There is nothing that can 
be done! It's impossible!</i>

00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:30.020
Th-These idiots...

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:34.440
Well, of course. After all, right now,

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:40.000
they're happy family men 
with millions in the bank.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:44.700
That guy is a major leaguer, which even a 
time machine could never help him become,

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:48.090
with an annual salary of 15 million dollars.

00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:50.460
No way is that enough to snap him out of it.

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:54.570
Now, hang on. That's just in the game...

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:59.550
They're escaping, sir, 
into their fantasy life.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.750
They're having trouble distinguishing 
reality from the game.

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:05.230
If anything, they might 
consider the game more real.

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:07.490
<b>Psst...</b>

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:08.730
What do we do?

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:13.480
Just leave it to me, sir.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.740
Wow, you guys are raking it in, huh?

00:18:24.690 --> 00:18:26.610
How's it going? You having fun?

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:27.580
Yeah...

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:28.750
I see.

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:33.750
But what would you do if I said I knew 
about a game that's even better?

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.830
What're you talking about?

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.790
What kind of game?

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:41.170
It's a game where pieces of 
scum try to outdo each other,

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:44.260
trap each other... a real diabolical one.

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.460
Wow.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:51.740
However, it's really difficult. 
You could call it extreme hard mode.

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:53.290
What game is that?

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:54.360
Sounds interesting.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:55.880
I wanna try!

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.440
<i>Well done, Endou.</i>

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:03.160
<i>You know from personal experience the exact 
kind of talk that debtors want to hear...</i>

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:07.410
Let me enlighten you. 
The name of this game is...

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:09.910
<i>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!</i>

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.790
Reality!

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:16.130
Let me introduce your opponents.

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:28.520
Every business he's invested in has failed. 
The man with no eye for potential:

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:31.560
The team of Ohmura, the maniacal investor.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.470
Despite having an annual income of zero yen,

00:19:33.470 --> 00:19:35.490
the cash he sinks into customizing his car

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:39.820
amounts to over a million a month! 
Custom Yamaguchi and his team!

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.790
He just can't forget the good old days.

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:46.830
The agent of the 80s, 
Bubble Kawakami and his team!

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.520
The man who ordered too much 
product, and sold far too little.

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:53.960
The man whose aim is terminally 
off, E.B.I. Nakane and his team!

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:58.960
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:01.970
I expected something like this to happen,

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:05.790
so I recruited a few other 
debtors to put these together...

00:20:05.790 --> 00:20:07.470
Four teams' worth.

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:13.480
They might've been reluctant to take action 
when surrounded by their peers, but now?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:19.480
Naturally, they'll be forced to 
engage in a bloody team battle.

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:27.990
The question now is: 
who will be the winning team?

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:32.760
<i>No! That's not how Restricted 
Rock-Paper-Scissors works!</i>

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:36.420
<i>The second day of rehearsal is a failure!</i>

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.810
<i>The training of the new hires is reloaded!</i>

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.760
<i>Tough luck, Tonegawa.</i>

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:45.510
<i>Tough luck, rookies.</i>

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.050
<i>Tough luck, Endou.</i>

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:52.390
<i>Tough luck to those of 
you in the tables, too.</i>

00:20:55.860 --> 00:21:00.820
<i>But hang in there, Tonegawa. 
Don't give up, Tonegawa.</i>

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:07.400
<i>This is the story of a lone man 
who struggles between his employer</i>

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:11.490
<i>and his own employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:15.970
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:55.260 --> 00:22:57.670
<i>Next time: "Business Trip"!</i>

00:22:56.120 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Business Trip</b>
